cy during the transition from colonial rule to self-governance. They played a key role in the establishment of the Tinkhundla administrative system.","royal_connection":"Traditional advisors to the royal inner council during the post-independence governance transition","founding_era":"Post-independence (1968–2018)","lineage_title":"The Independence and Nation Building Lineage"},"vector":{"1968":0.04446234686411523,"2018":0.0586082076918692,"tfwala":0.1172164153837384,"clan":0.07981679367458924,"independ":0.17582462307560762,"nation":0.06608323299617239,"build":0.0586082076918692,"lineag":0.03618754873945881,"tradit":0.03618754873945881,"advisor":0.05033340956721279,"royal":0.022041687911704824,"inner":0.0586082076918692,"council":0.1172164153837384,"dure":0.060632972072722474,"post":0.1172164153837384,"govern":0.08892469372823046,"transit":0.1172164153837384,"serv":0.03990839683729462,"within":0.05033340956721279,"swazi":0.030316486036361237,"known":0.05033340956721279,"libandla":0.0586082076918692,"advis":0.05033340956721279,"monarchi":0.05033340956721279,"matter":0.0586082076918692,"law":0.0586082076918692,"land":0.03990839683729462,"cultur":0.03990839683729462,"polici":0.0586082076918692,"coloni":0.03990839683729462,"rule":0.04446234686411523,"self":0.0586082076918692,"plai":0.0586082076918692,"kei":0.0586082076918692,"role":0.04446234686411523,"establish":0.0586082076918692,"tinkhundla":0.0586082076918692,"administr":0.0586082076918692,"system":0.0586082076918692}},{"type":"song","data":{"title":"Siyilandela Inkhosi","description":"A sacred Incwala song sung by warriors as they march to the royal cattle byre. It praises the king and calls on the ancestors to strengthen the nation. This song is only sung during Incwala and is considered spiritually powerful.","ceremony_name":"Incwala — First Fruits Ceremony"},"vector":{"siyilandela":0.09902766127246866,"inkhosi":0.09902766127246866,"incwala":0.20229428741663136,"first":0.0751260343566085,"fruit":0.075126034356608